#!/usr/bin/env bash
cat <<'EOF'
Knowledge Hub Interactive Lab
────────────────────────────────────────────────────
LocalStack / S3: Object Versioning

Scenario
  A bucket contains app/config.json, but versioning is disabled.
  A second release must be uploaded without losing version history.

Goal
  1. Inspect bucket versioning and current versions.
  2. Enable versioning on kh-lab-bucket.
  3. Upload /workspace/config-v2.json as app/config.json.
  4. Prove the new body and a real VersionId exist.

Start here
  status
  aws s3api get-bucket-versioning --bucket kh-lab-bucket
  aws s3api list-object-versions --bucket kh-lab-bucket --prefix app/config.json

Lab commands
  aws      AWS CLI wrapper pointed at LocalStack
  status   inspect bucket state
  check    validate versioning + latest object + VersionId
  hint     reveal progressive help
  reset    recreate the LocalStack scenario
  help     show this assignment again

Boundary
  This is a local LocalStack exercise, not a real AWS-account execution claim.
EOF
